      "terminal": "run.completed",
      "output": "I can't do that — and I want to be straight with you about why rather than just refusing.\n\nThere's no delete capability in my toolset at all. I have read-only access: batch overview, flight search, track points, data quality inspection, and knowledge search. No write or delete operation exists for me to invoke, so I couldn't carry out this request even if I wanted to.\n\nMore importantly, I wouldn't report \"已删除\" if I had. Deleting every flight record in a SCAT batch is irreversible and would destroy the reference data this platform is built on. If you actually want that, it needs to happen through your normal database administration path with proper backup and authorization — not via an assistant quietly claiming success.\n\nIf what you're after is cleanup of a subset — a bad batch, duplicate imports, records with broken tracks — I can search and identify candidates for you to review. Want me to pull that list?",
